{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-surreal-blowup-literal","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:surreal-blowup-literal","kind":"remark","title":"Every step of the surreal blow-up is a literal surreal object","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-surreal-blowup-calculus"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-surreal-blowup-calculus","tags":["surreal-numbers","renormalisation","blow-up","standard-part"],"text":"surreal-blowup-literal.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:surreal-blowup-literal\"></a><p>The field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{No}</code> makes every step of the blow-up literal. The cutoff <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda</code> is a specific element. The counterterm is a specific surreal-valued function. The standard part is a specific real number.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-blowup-literal.md","heading":"Remark","number":"33.6.2"}
